 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Holes:** Holes appear if the voxels generated from the four corners of a subpatch are not N-adjacent. The algorithm prevents this by recursively subdividing until the N-adjacency condition is met [S1].
-*   **Shared Boundaries:** Shared boundaries between patches or subpatches must map to the same voxel to ensure leak-free results. The algorithm guarantees this because shared boundary points are evaluated at the same parameter coordinates [S1].
-*   **Precision:** The voxel coordinate conversion uses `floor(S(u,v).x + 0.5)`. Floating-point precision errors in surface evaluation could theoretically cause boundary voxels to be assigned incorrectly, but the recursive subdivision ensures that adjacent patches share evaluation points, mitigating gaps [S1].
